From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:32:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 120/141] feat(refinery): run the merge-push step through
 merge-push.sh and retire the formula's lane (gcp-l8td.6)

B1 phase 3, step 3 (gcp-l8td.3 DESIGN). The refinery hand-rendered the merge
lane from 14 fenced blocks of mol-refinery-patrol's merge-push step on every
patrol, about 30% of its tool calls and the source of two silent render bugs.
gcp-l8td.5 added merge-push.sh and proved it matches that lane; this switches
the step over and deletes the formula copy.

The merge-push step is now one sentinelled invoke block: locate the script from
the formula's own resolved source (GC_PACK_DIR only as a fallback, fail closed
with a drain-ack when neither resolves), run `"$MERGE_PUSH" --work "$WORK"`
with no other flags, and act on the exit status. 0 and 4 continue; 9 pours the
next wisp, assigns it with the session-iteration stamp, burns this one and
drains; 11 stops without touching the bead; anything else drains. The step
prose keeps the full status table and the status-7 guidance. Two deviations
from "verbatim relocation", both forced by "the block contains no {{": the
status-9 pour reads rig, target and binding prefix back from the script's own
`merge-push: config` line instead of rendering {{rig_name}} etc., and it drops
block_existing_pr's `echo "$reason"` because the script already printed it.

Tests. test_refinery_merge_push, _already_merged and _origin_repo now source
merge-push.sh with MERGE_PUSH_SOURCE_ONLY=1 instead of extracting formula
blocks; assertions are unchanged. The origin-repo and gate seams needed two
small harness changes: already_merged stops lane_direct at direct_close and
sets the CFG_* values resolve_config would have, and origin_repo sources the
script's resolve_origin_repo. test_merge_approval_gate.sh keeps its 16 gate
cases byte-identical, re-points the resolution and parking cases to the script
(the gate is found as the script's sibling, so the city-scripts-dir fallback
case is deleted), and the whole-lane status 4 stays with the lane suite's
4b_refused_parks. The lane suite loses its formula adapter and the stitching;
every case now runs the formula's extracted invoke block, so the status table
is the real one, and two cases pin the locator (formula source wins over
GC_PACK_DIR; nothing resolving drains and touches nothing): 25 cases.

Two suites outside the bead's file list also read the deleted lane text and had
to follow it: test_gastown_pack_assets.sh (the direct-lane safety assertions
now read merge-push.sh) and test_refinery_reject_branch_survival.sh (the
merged-path deletion gate is checked in the script; no formula step may delete
a branch).

The inference gate splits its contracts: the lane fragments moved to a
script-file contract for merge-push.sh, and the formula keeps merge-push.sh and
--work "$WORK". The refinery prompt now says merge-push.sh chains
--unset-metadata rejection_reason.

Validation: every gastown/tests/*.sh exits 0; pytest tests/ has one failure,
the pre-existing docs/design bare-bd violation (gcp-98gh).

