-  Without `fork_sha` recorded, neither arm can fire: stay conservative and fall
-  through to the false-completion guard.
-- **False completion (halt):** a branch that introduces no change vs its
-  merge-base is definitionally not a merge. Refuse it before touching `$TARGET`.
-  Legit no-op resolutions use wontfix/duplicate/not-planned, never merged — so
-  this never blocks a real merge. The fork point is what keeps the content arm
-  above from swallowing this case: a genuinely empty branch has no diff against
-  its own `fork_sha`, and a branch merely rebased onto newer target carries no
-  commit the target lacks (gcp-duy), so neither reaches the already-merged
-  close.
