-  `set -e` and relied on it to stop after a failed `git merge --ff-only`. It
-  did not propagate through the refinery's execution harness, so execution
-  continued into the metadata write and `gc bd close`. A step that mutates
-  bead state must never depend on shell-option inheritance across a harness
